{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSED. Gerrit 1708 merged as 1c3e945cb8 on main (Gerrit rebased server-side over sibling acouchi's structured_run split, c3d5c5c8fa; the local pre-rebase sha was 6c62cfb9ff). Both gates green before submit: LLM-Review +1 (rebar-review-bot, PASS, 3 resolved advisories) and Verified +1 (rebar-ci-bot, run 31673250339 success — lint+typecheck, pytest on ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos py3.13, optionality, artifact-probe, eval-discipline, verify-identity, golden-path, pip-audit, mutation shard select). All 7 ACs ticked.\n\nTwo operational notes for siblings still in flight:\n- The complexity-baseline diff landed as a pure 4-line DELETION and CI's baseline lock accepted it, confirming that draining an entry below the threshold is treated as shrink-only. No rebase-regeneration was needed: acouchi landed first and did not touch the baseline file, so the epic's anticipated regenerate-on-conflict step never triggered for this change.\n- The globally-installed rebar (auto-updating dev build at c6828ef) is BROKEN for close: 'ImportError: cannot import name commit_impact from rebar._engine_support' raised from close_precheck._check_file_impact_vs_diff. The worktree's own editable build closes fine, so this is stale-global-vs-main drift, not a store problem. Use 'env PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH rebar ...' for closes until the hourly LaunchAgent resyncs."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786604600087428001,"uuid":"ea72ac8e-b5ca-4042-92bf-3a20635ba071"}